{"path":"types/numeric_limits/lowest","title":"std::numeric_limits<T>::lowest","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::numeric_limits&lt;T&gt;::</span>lowest","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/lowest","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"Returns the lowest finite value representable by the numeric type T, that is, a finite value x such that there is no other finite value y where y < x.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">static</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T lowest<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the lowest finite value representable by the numeric type <code>T</code>, that is, a finite value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> such that there is no other finite value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y</span></code> where <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">y <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> x</span></code>. This is different from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">min</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> for floating-point types. Only meaningful for bounded types.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td>  <code>T</code>\n</td>\n<td